        "original_id": "116e3957-6b4a-57d1-8faf-7adc98540da7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Sinfield\n- Places: AJ Bell Stadium, Salford City Stadium, Barton-upon-Irwell, Eccles, Salford, England\n- Organizations: Salford Red Devils, Leeds, Super League\n- Awards: Lance Todd Trophy, Harry Sunderland Trophy, Golden Boot, Challenge Cup\n\nFacts:\n- The Lance Todd Trophy is presented at a celebratory dinner at the AJ Bell Stadium, which is the home of the Salford Red Devils.\n- The Salford City Stadium is referred to as the AJ Bell Stadium for sponsorship purposes and is a rugby stadium in Barton-upon-Irwell, Eccles, Salford, England.\n- Kevin Sinfield played his entire professional career with Leeds.\n- Kevin Sinfield is one of the most successful players in Super League history.\n- Kevin Sinfield captained Leeds to seven Super League championships and two Challenge Cup successes.\n- In 2005, Kevin Sinfield won the Lance Todd Trophy.\n- In 2009 and 2012, Kevin Sinfield won the Harry Sunderland Trophy.\n- In 2012, Kevin Sinfield won the Golden Boot and became one of only four British-based players to achieve that award.",
